<task id="031" project="spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>preference≠permission negative test; not-a-second-decider</title>
    <phase>4: User Model</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>2</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>030</dependencies>
    <blocks>none</blocks>
    <tags>testing, unit-test, integration-test, bff-api</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>TEST-MODIFYING override — any tests/** task runs FULL rigor unconditionally.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified assertion test against a known contract (AgentToolFilterContext members); low ambiguity.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>4</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Author the negative test that mechanically enforces preference≠permission and not-a-second-decider: assert AgentToolFilterContext carries no profile/memory-derived members, and that the profile fragment never grants a capability (grounding still gates). Assert the chip reorder is deterministic + preference-keyed with no model call.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE test engineer expert in the dispatch spine, AgentToolFilterContext, and ADR-039 invariants.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A passing negative test proving (1) AgentToolFilterContext has no profile/memory-derived members, (2) an injected profile does not flip any dispatch/grounding decision, and (3) chip reorder is deterministic + preference-keyed (no model call).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      This is the mechanical proof of FR-E3/E4 and the ADR-039 project-scoped constraint. It guards against the User Model quietly becoming a second decider.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/AgentToolProjection.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">preference ≠ permission; ONE decider. The test MUST fail if a profile-derived member appears in AgentToolFilterContext or if profile injection changes a grounding decision.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Prefer unit + seam; no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration/ctor-null tests.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Enumerate AgentToolFilterContext members; assert none are profile/memory-derived.</step>
    <step order="2">Add a test: with vs without an injected profile, the set of grounded tools is identical.</step>
    <step order="3">Add a test: chip reorder is deterministic + preference-keyed (same input → same order; no model call).</step>
    <step order="4">Run; ensure red-before-green semantics (test would fail if a profile member leaked in).</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md 031 → ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Run unit + seam tests</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/ (preference≠permission negative test)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A test asserts AgentToolFilterContext carries no profile/memory-derived members.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test asserts profile injection does not change the grounded-tool set.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test asserts chip reorder is deterministic + preference-keyed with no model call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All added tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Spec FR-E3 / FR-E4. TEST-MODIFYING rigor override applies.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load knowledge/files. FULL-rigor Step 9.5 (TEST-MODIFYING override).</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
